{"chunk_id": "476db68a8c60", "text": "After Brahma departs, King Bhagiratha performs extreme penance to persuade Shiva to receive the descending celestial river Ganga, whose fall would otherwise shatter the earth. Standing on one toe for a year, living only on air, he wins Shiva\u2019s favor. When Ganga finally plunges from heaven with immense force, she arrogantly thinks she can sweep Shiva away\u2014but the god traps the entire torrent within his tangled locks. The river remains imprisoned there for ages until Bhagiratha performs further austerities. Shiva then releases her gently, dividing her into seven streams. One follows Bhagiratha\u2019s chariot across the earth while gods, sages, and celestial beings gather in aerial vehicles to witness the cosmic event. The descent of Ganga becomes a moment of purification, freeing cursed beings and linking heaven, earth, and the divine.\nAfter Bhagiratha\u2019s penance, Shiva releases the Ganga from his hair, splitting it into seven streams as it follows Bhagiratha to earth.\nThemes: divine intervention, penance and devotion, descent of the Ganges, cosmic spectacle, purification", "vector": [0.013951768167316914, -0.001232923474162817, 0.0044290791265666485, 0.027080463245511055, 0.005171194672584534, 0.021372921764850616, -0.02361276000738144, 0.005505146458745003, -0.021534837782382965, -0.023572281002998352, 0.0019514260347932577, 0.021696753799915314, -0.002502952702343464, 0.02874010242521763, 0.0010659474646672606, -0.0014741108752787113, 0.03993929922580719, -0.013951768167316914, 0.02984653040766716, -0.0011190761579200625, 0.012987018562853336, -0.0035115547943860292, 0.00325181451626122, 0.02644629217684269, -0.0409647673368454, 0.004024289082735777, 0.033462654799222946, -0.030332278460264206, 0.007839436642825603, 0.0009133078856393695, -0.0150716882199049, -0.005032891407608986, -0.017905218526721, -0.002809918485581875, 0.0007931357831694186, -0.006223649252206087, -0.011340871453285217, -0.00472929887473583